{
  "id": "15-part-tree-over-all-deformers",
  "description": "One part transform over each of the four deformers, to pin that the tree composes on the OUTSIDE of every one of them uniformly. The mesh part is the load-bearing member: it has no single joint transform to fold into, only one per bone blended per vertex, so a kernel that tried to compose the part tree INSIDE the deformer could not produce this case's output at all. Every part here is also driven by a bound joint or a bone chain, so this is the 'both' case -- the joint deforms the artwork, the tree then carries the deformed result. A non-uniform destination scale is applied on top, because the tree runs in source pixels and the surface scale must still be the last multiply.",
